  "body": "Tender: Closes on Wednesday 28 October 2026 at 2:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nSet on a lovely, level freehold site of approximately 700m², widely regarded as one of New Zealand's most desirable forms of property ownership. This character 1920s bungalow offers an exciting combination of character, space, and future potential.\r\n\r\nFrom the home, you can enjoy views towards Mount Victoria, North Head and glimpses of the water, a wonderful reminder of just how special this location is and how close you are to the water. Narrow Neck Beach, Waitimata Golf Course, and parks are an easy walk away.\r\n\r\nInside, the home retains its original charm, with beautiful native timber flooring, 3 double bedrooms and comfortable open-plan living. The living, kitchen and dining areas flow naturally out to the deck, then down into the spacious back garden, creating an easy connection between indoor and outdoor living.\r\n\r\nAnd it’s the land that really adds another dimension. With 700m² of level freehold land, there is plenty of room to enjoy the home as it is, while also giving you the opportunity to extend and enhance the existing accommodation in the future. There’s still ample space for gardens, outdoor entertaining and potentially even a swimming pool.\r\n\r\nWhether you’re looking for a comfortable 1920s home, a project to add value over time, or simply a property with the space and potential to create something truly special, 15 Aramoana Avenue deserves your attention.\r\n\r\nThis home suits a range of buyers, from young families to downsizers, builders looking to add on or add a second dwelling, and landlords, as it already has great tenants who would be happy to stay on.\r\n\r\nWith the land, the views and the location, the potential here is undeniable; now it’s up to you to make it your own.",
